.Dd $Mdocdate: November 23 2026 $
.Dt DCARPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dcarpd
.Nd distribute a dynamic carp address to backup hosts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dnv
.Op Fl c Ar control_socket
.Op Fl f Ar state_file
.Op Fl g Ar backup_gateway
.Fl i Ar interface
.Op Fl k Ar key_file
.Op Fl s Ar sync_interface
.Op Fl x Ar program
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon implements the Distributed Common Address Redundancy Protocol
.Pq DCARP
for a
.Xr carp 4
interface whose IPv4 address the master typically gets from
.Xr dhcpleased 8 .
As master, it gives the address to the backups.
On every host,
.Nm
writes the configuration it holds to a state file, from which
.Xr ifstated 8
or a program run by
.Nm
sets the routes;
.Nm
changes no routes itself.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar control_socket
Use
.Ar control_socket
instead of the default
.Pa /dev/dhcpleased.sock
to communicate with
.Xr dhcpleased 8 .
.It Fl d
Do not daemonize.
If this option is specified,
.Nm
will run in the foreground and log to
.Em stderr .
Without this option,
.Nm
sends log messages to
.Xr syslog 3 .
.It Fl f Ar state_file
Use
.Ar state_file
as the state file instead of the default
.Pa /var/db/dcarpd/ Ns Ar interface .
.It Fl g Ar backup_gateway
This host's IPv4 address on another network the hosts share, typically
the internal one, for the others to use as gateway while this host is
master.
.It Fl i Ar interface
The
.Xr carp 4
interface whose IPv4 address the hosts share.
It must have exactly one
.Cm vhid .
.It Fl k Ar key_file
Read the shared key from
.Ar key_file
instead of the default
.Pa /etc/dcarp.key .
The key is the SHA-256 hash of the first 4096 bytes of the file and
must be the same on all hosts;
.Nm
logs a fingerprint of it when it reads the file.
The file must not be readable by group or others, and must be owned by
root unless
.Fl n
is given.
.It Fl n
Do not change the addresses of the interface or any carp demote
counter, and do not require root.
.Nm
still sends messages as master, writes the state file and runs
.Ar program .
.It Fl s Ar sync_interface
Send and receive the messages on
.Ar sync_interface
instead of on
.Ar interface .
All hosts must use the same network for them.
.It Fl v
Also log messages of priority debug.
.It Fl x Ar program
Run
.Ar program ,
the absolute path of an executable, whenever
.Nm
writes the state file or puts the address back, and when the
.Xr carp 4
state of the interface changes.
Its arguments are the state file and the current carp state:
.Cm MASTER ,
.Cm BACKUP
or
.Cm INIT .
Runs do not overlap: requests made while one is running are combined
into a single run when it exits.
.Nm
does not wait for them, and logs failures.
.El
.Pp
As master,
.Nm
sends its configuration: the address and netmask of the interface, the
gateway of that network
.Pq normally that of its default route through the interface ,
its
.Ar backup_gateway ,
how long the DHCP lease lasts, and the generation.
Each message also carries the sender's
.Xr carp 4
priority.
It sends a message when it starts or becomes master, when another
program changes the address, and every 10 seconds.
The messages are encrypted and authenticated with XChaCha20-Poly1305
using the shared key, and sent as UDP datagrams to the multicast group
224.0.0.18, port 3522, on the interface or
.Ar sync_interface .
.Pp
The generation is the time the address was obtained or its DHCP lease
last renewed.
A change of the address that
.Nm
did not make starts a new generation, and so does each acknowledgement
of the lease.
The master reads the lease from
.Xr dhcpleased 8
before each message, as
.Ql dhcpleasectl -l
does;
.Nm
never requests a new lease.
At startup the generation is that in the state file, or 0 if the file is
missing or the interface has another address.
.Pp
.Nm
accepts only messages that arrive on the interface it sends on,
authenticate, are not replays, and carry a timestamp within 30 seconds
of its clock, so the clocks of the hosts must agree within 30 seconds.
It takes a configuration of a newer generation than its own and rejects
one of an older generation.
A master takes a configuration of the same generation only from a
sender with a better priority: a lower demote count, or else a lower
.Cm advbase ,
or else a lower
.Cm advskew ,
with ties broken by a random sender id.
A host that is not master takes it from any sender.
To take a configuration,
.Nm
makes its address the only IPv4 address of the interface and writes the
state file.
Rejected messages are logged with their source address, at most one
every 10 seconds.
.Pp
As backup,
.Nm
puts the address back whenever the interface has no IPv4 address, for
example after
.Xr dhcpleased 8
removed it at the expiry of a lease obtained while the host was master.
It never does so as master.
.Pp
While the interface has no IPv4 address,
.Nm
increases the carp demote counter of every group of the interface by
one, among them
.Ql carp
and
.Ql all ,
which demotes every
.Xr carp 4
interface of the host.
It decreases them again when the interface has an address.
.Pp
The state file holds
.Xr sh 1
variable assignments.
.Nm
replaces it atomically whenever the configuration it sends or takes
changes, as at a lease renewal, and reads it when it starts.
.Bl -tag -width DCARP_BACKUP_GATEWAY
.It Va DCARP_INTERFACE
The interface.
.It Va DCARP_ADDRESS
The shared IPv4 address.
.It Va DCARP_NETMASK
Its netmask.
.It Va DCARP_GATEWAY
The gateway to use as master, or empty.
.It Va DCARP_BACKUP_GATEWAY
The gateway to use as backup: the
.Ar backup_gateway
of the master whose configuration
.Nm
last took, or empty.
.It Va DCARP_GENERATION
The generation, in seconds since the Epoch, or 0 if unknown.
.It Va DCARP_LEASE_TIME
How long the DHCP lease lasts from the generation on, in seconds,
or empty if unknown.
.It Va DCARP_LEASE_EXPIRES
When the lease runs out, in seconds since the Epoch, or empty.
.El
.Pp
Upon receiving
.Dv SIGHUP ,
.Nm
rereads the key file, keeping the old key if that fails, and resumes
reading the lease from
.Xr dhcpleased 8
if it had stopped; see
.Sx CAVEATS .
Upon receiving
.Dv SIGTERM ,
it lifts any demotion it holds and exits.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/examples/ifstated-dcarpd.conf" -compact
.It Pa /dev/dhcpleased.sock
Default
.Ux Ns -domain
socket used for communication with
.Xr dhcpleased 8 .
.It Pa /etc/dcarp.key
Default shared key file.
.It Pa /etc/examples/ifstated-dcarpd.conf
Example
.Xr ifstated.conf 5
for a pair of hosts.
.It Pa /var/db/dcarpd/ Ns Ar interface
Default state file.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create the key on one host and copy it unchanged to the others:
.Pp
.Dl # (umask 077; openssl rand -hex 32 > /etc/dcarp.key)
.Pp
Let the messages through in
.Xr pf.conf 5 :
.Pp
.Dl pass quick proto udp to 224.0.0.18 port 3522
.Pp
Run
.Nm
for carp0 on each host, with its own address on the internal network:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# rcctl enable dcarpd
# rcctl set dcarpd flags -i carp0 -g 192.168.1.2
# rcctl start dcarpd
.Ed
.Pp
For a pair of hosts,
.Xr ifstated 8
can set the routes from the state file; see
.Pa /etc/examples/ifstated-dcarpd.conf .
With more than two hosts, a backup must also follow a new master while
it stays backup; set the routes with a program given with
.Fl x
instead, such as this
.Pa /etc/dcarpd-route :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#!/bin/sh
\&. "$1" || exit 1
case $2 in
MASTER)	gw=$DCARP_GATEWAY ;;
BACKUP)	gw=$DCARP_BACKUP_GATEWAY ;;
*)	exit 0 ;;
esac
[ -n "$gw" ] || exit 0
route -q change default $gw 2>/dev/null || route -q add default $gw
.Ed
.Pp
Make it executable, and add
.Fl x Pa /etc/dcarpd-route
to the flags of every host.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr carp 4 ,
.Xr ifstated.conf 5 ,
.Xr pf.conf 5 ,
.Xr dhcpleasectl 8 ,
.Xr dhcpleased 8 ,
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ifstated 8 ,
.Xr ntpd 8 ,
.Xr rcctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Ox 7.4 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The
.Nm
program was written by
.An Niklas Hallqvist .
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm
reads the DHCP lease with control messages internal to
.Xr dhcpleased 8 ,
and must be built from the same source tree.
After an answer it does not expect, or none within a second, it logs
this and does not read the lease again until
.Dv SIGHUP ;
renewals then start no new generations and do not update the lease
times in the state files.
.Pp
If
.Nm
exits other than on
.Dv SIGTERM
while it holds a demotion, the demotion remains; lift it with
.Ic ifconfig Fl g Ar group Cm -carpdemote
for each group of the interface, including
.Ql all .
.Sh BUGS
.Nm
ignores
.Dv SIGINT .
